  "provenance": {
    "source": "Aggregate statistics from 9 public ONT R10.4.1 MUC1 amplicon libraries, ENA PRJEB92208 (Madritsch et al. 2025, Sci Rep, doi:10.1038/s41598-025-30441-3). No reads or sequences are included.",
    "derived_by": "MucOneSpan deep review 2026-09-23 (read-level profiling against per-sample POA consensus); errors and stutter derived and validated with helpers/calibrate_read_profile.py --engine empirical; stutter refit for every per-strand target key with n >= 500 (adds C8, the dupC run) and stutter_fallback added for unfitted runs (MucOneUp #132), validated on a dupC amplicon template with 4000 molecules; v2 (MucOneUp #131): errors.strand_rates fitted per read strand with helpers/calibrate_read_profile.py --engine empirical --fit-strand-rates 3 against error_rates_per_ref_base['<strand>:<type>'] (MucOneSpan benchsim targets prjeb92208_v1.json, which reproduce v1's errors and stutter exactly), on a 4.05 kb simulated MUC1 amplicon template (MucSim-Bench v4 standard case dev-standard-ont_amplicon_r10-0001, haplotype 1 of its *.simulated.fa, slice [9994:14044]); everything else is unchanged from ont_r10_sup_amplicon_v1; v3 (MucOneUp #131): molecules.unit_stutter_rate/unit_stutter_pmf (whole-repeat-unit PCR slippage) fitted with the same command plus --fit-unit-stutter from per_allele_stutter_and_length_noise (18 alleles, 9 libraries); everything else is unchanged from ont_r10_sup_amplicon_v2; v4 (MucOneUp #131): errors.strand_rates refitted with --fit-strand-rates 3 on a template whose homopolymer runs match the target (MucSim-Bench v4 standard case dev-standard-ont_amplicon_r10-0002, haplotype 1 of its *.simulated.fa, slice [9994:14404], 73 units: 0.626 C7 runs per 60 bp against 0.622 in the target; the v2 template has about 0.54, so its + strand deletion rate came out 7% high on real-like alleles), and molecules.unit_stutter_rate/unit_stutter_pmf refitted with --fit-unit-stutter 3 --vntr 6 4386, so that simulated reads reproduce the real profiler's per-allele stutter ratios (which also count the peak's own indel tail); --n-molecules 12000; everything else is unchanged from ont_r10_sup_amplicon_v3",
